      "side": 1,
      "message": "Quick scanning of this change I agree that we do not want to add another Ref count to the DawnTexture class. IMO Skia has the correct set of ref counting needed on our internal objects and all the appropriate mechanisms to notify clients when things are safe to be destroyed. I agree with Michael that if Chrome is using BackendTexture they should also be using the ReleaseProcs when wrapping into an SkImage to know when it is safe to destroy the BackendTexture.",
